 ALTERNATIVES: moving `_serve_supervisor` out of the CLI into a callable, rejected because it is the supervisor's lifecycle code the feature file puts out of reach and its refusals are process exits; running the staging copy, rejected because it holds no installed dependencies and may already be released; importing `dev_server` to start the runtime in process, rejected for the same reach and because it would bring `subprocess` under the door once the door records requests.
 
 HOW TO REVERSE: delete `packages/orchestration/preview_control.py`, `packages/orchestration/preview_runner.py`, `apps/cli/commands/job_preview_cmd.py`, their three test files, the two catalog entries, the registration in `apps/cli/commands/__init__.py`, the two rows of `docs/guides/exit-codes.md` and the three allowlist lines, and this paragraph.
+
+## DECISION F041 D4 — the write door records a preview request and hands the job to the UI server's own preview worker, whose thread runs the harness's verbs, probes every live preview again each fifteen seconds, stops one nobody has viewed for `preview.idle_ttl_seconds`, and stops them all when the server closes; the app card reads `/api/jobs/<id>/preview`, which counts as a view and shows a link only while live (2026-09-29)
+
+CONTEXT: DECISION F041 D3 (5) left the door's commands, the step acting on them, the revalidation of a live preview and the idle stop to this round. Measured by the reviewer at `468b3a36`: `_handle_command_submission` in `packages/orchestration/ui_server.py` runs every effect inside the request, in the order effect, audit line, publication; `TestCommandDoorImportGuard` of `tests/ui_server/test_command_channel.py` pins the door's imports by equality and forbids `subprocess` among them; `UI_EXPOSED_COMMANDS` in `apps/cli/command_catalog.py` is pinned as a sorted literal; the server has no thread of its own; and `start_ui_server` blocks in `serve_forever` and closes the server in a `finally`.
+
+CHOSEN: (1) THE DOOR maps `job.preview-start` and `job.preview-stop` to `preview_control.request_preview`, its one new import, and answers 200 `accepted` with the recorded state; a request never declines. It then hands the job id to the handler's `preview_worker`, when one is set, and runs no verb itself. (2) THE WORKER is `packages/orchestration/preview_worker.py`, one per server, created and started by `start_ui_server` after its socket is bound and closed in its `finally`. `submit` queues a job and wakes the thread; `step` acts on every queued request with `run_pending`, then for every preview it keeps live stops it when idle and otherwise probes it again, one that no longer answers losing its link as `failed` with "the app stopped answering: <message>" and being stopped; the thread steps when woken and at least every `PREVIEW_TICK_SECONDS`, fifteen. `adopt_live` takes on every preview a record already calls live, so a restarted server still looks after it, and `close` stops every preview the worker keeps live. The worker looks the runner up in `preview_runner` at each call. (3) THE IDLE STOP: `preview.idle_ttl_seconds`, default 900, zero or less meaning never; the clock is the record's `viewed_at`, which a live preview gets when it goes live and at every read of `/api/jobs/<id>/preview`; an idle preview is stopped with the reason "stopped after <n> seconds without a viewer". (4) THE VIEW: `preview_view` answers the link and port only while the state is `live`, whatever the stored record holds.
+
+ALTERNATIVES: running `run_pending` inside the door's request, rejected because a serve may take ninety seconds and the door's import guard forbids the process launcher it would reach; a separate process started by `remedy ui`, rejected because nothing would then stop its previews when the server closes and it would need its own lifecycle; a new event on the job's stream for each preview state, rejected for now because the card reads one small view and every new event name needs its humanize entry and its readers named, which T003 can add if the card needs them; revalidating by reading `runtime.json` rather than probing, rejected because a running record says nothing about whether the app still answers.
+
+HOW TO REVERSE: delete `packages/orchestration/preview_worker.py` and its test, the door clause, `_dispatch_job_preview`, the `preview` endpoint, the worker in `start_ui_server`, the two ids in `UI_EXPOSED_COMMANDS`, the config key and its guide line, the additions to `preview_control.py` and their tests, the guard edits in `tests/ui_server/test_command_channel.py` and `tests/ui_server/test_preview_commands.py`, and this paragraph.
